## Purpose and audience

Purpose: the behavior asserted in this spec  Audience: engineers reading this spec to confirm the behavior still holds.

## Operator workflow

1. Run `bin/simple test test/01_unit/compiler/interpreter/implicit_self_field_assign_spec.spl`.
2. Every scenario must pass; a failure is a regression in the behavior under test.

## Compatibility and limitations

Covers the behavior asserted here; platform-specific behavior is out of scope.

## Scenarios

### implicit-self field assignment in a me method

#### rejects a bare field assignment instead of silently discarding it

- Verify: rejects a bare field assignment instead of silently discarding it


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 7 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: rejects a bare field assignment instead of silently discarding it")
val path = write_case("implicit", IMPLICIT_SRC)
val (_output, code) = run_case(path)
# The core regression: the old build exited 0 having printed
# IMPLICIT_RESULT=false, i.e. the mutation was silently dropped.
assert_not_equal(code, 0)
```

</details>

#### never reports the silently-unmutated field value

- Verify: never reports the silently-unmutated field value


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 4 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: never reports the silently-unmutated field value")
val path = write_case("implicit_value", IMPLICIT_SRC)
assert_equal(output_match_count(path, "IMPLICIT_RESULT=false"), "0")
```

</details>

#### names the shadowed field and points at the self. form

- Verify: names the shadowed field and points at the self. form


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 6 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: names the shadowed field and points at the self. form")
val path = write_case("implicit_msg", IMPLICIT_SRC)
val (output, _code) = run_case(path)
assert_contains(output, "is a field of")
assert_contains(output, "self.flag")
```

</details>

#### still applies an explicit self.field assignment

- Verify: still applies an explicit self.field assignment


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 6 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: still applies an explicit self.field assignment")
val path = write_case("explicit", EXPLICIT_SRC)
val (output, code) = run_case(path)
assert_contains(output, "EXPLICIT_RESULT=true")
assert_equal(code, 0)
```

</details>

#### leaves a bare non-field local assignment working

